1
00:00:00,910 --> 00:00:08,020
Divide one decimal number by one decimal number

2
00:00:08,020 --> 00:00:16,620
Calculate 30.24 divided by 8.4 we do as follows

3
00:00:16,620 --> 00:00:25,310
Decimal part of divisor 8.4 has one digit.

4
00:00:25,880 --> 00:00:42,310
Move comma of number 30.24 to right one digit to get 302.4; remove comma at number 8.4 to get 84.

5
00:00:42,310 --> 00:00:58,860
Perform division 302.4 divided by 84 according to dividing decimal number by whole number as above.

6
00:00:58,860 --> 00:01:10,800
So 30.24 divided by 8.4 equals 3.6.

7
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:19,370
Conclusion: To divide one decimal number by one decimal number we do as follows:

8
00:01:19,370 --> 00:01:38,800
Count how many digits in decimal part of divisor then move comma at dividend to right that many digits.

9
00:01:40,060 --> 00:01:56,570
Remove comma at divisor then perform division of decimal number divided by whole number.

10
00:01:58,040 --> 00:02:05,330
To firmly grasp rule we do following example:

11
00:02:05,330 --> 00:02:14,680
49.95 divided by 1.35

12
00:02:15,370 --> 00:02:30,750
Decimal part of both numbers 49.95 and 1.35 both have two digits, remove comma at both numbers we get 4995 and 135.

13
00:02:30,750 --> 00:02:43,970
Perform division 4995 divided by 135.

14
00:02:43,970 --> 00:02:54,060
So 49.95 divided by 1.35 equals 37.

